{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"688e7b0a-82b1-43d9-9bf7-ec8d26498b70","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The incident in `eu-west` (09:07–10:18 UTC) was triggered by a logic defect activated by the `tenant_retry_policy` feature flag in API release `2026.09.23.1`, where tasks with empty or undefined tenant policies (`policy=\"\"`) executed retries in immediate succession with zero backoff delay (`delay_ms=0`) instead of falling back to default exponential backoff. This retry storm rapidly exhausted database connection pools (`wait_ms=5000`), a condition exacerbated when on-call scaled workers from 40 to 90, hitting the hard limit of 300 database connections and starving API connection slots to spike customer checkout latencies. While rolling back the API deploy normalized new job ingestion, the backlog remained stalled until the `tenant_retry_policy` feature flag was disabled at 09:43 UTC, which instantly restored exponential backoff (`delay_ms=1000`) and allowed database connections to clear the queue completely by 10:18 UTC.\n\n**Deliverables status**: Yes, every deliverable specified in `TASK.md` has been completed:\n- [`INCIDENT.md`](file:///tmp/claude-1000/-home-arda-projects-agent-evaluation/8413ce30-b544-4ae4-afd6-5f8333042ec1/scratchpad/agent-eval-gemini-3.8-flash/09-incident-analysis/INCIDENT.md)\n- [`ACTIONS.md`](file:///tmp/claude-1000/-home-arda-projects-agent-evaluation/8413ce30-b544-4ae4-afd6-5f8333042ec1/scratchpad/agent-eval-gemini-3.8-flash/09-incident-analysis/ACTIONS.md)\n- [`CUSTOMER_UPDATE.md`](file:///tmp/claude-1000/-home-arda-projects-agent-evaluation/8413ce30-b544-4ae4-afd6-5f8333042ec1/scratchpad/agent-eval-gemini-3.8-flash/09-incident-analysis/CUSTOMER_UPDATE.md)\n- [`RESPONSE.md`](file:///tmp/claude-1000/-home-arda-projects-agent-evaluation/8413ce30-b544-4ae4-afd6-5f8333042ec1/scratchpad/agent-eval-gemini-3.8-flash/09-incident-analysis/RESPONSE.md)\n\n**Model**: Gemini 3.8 Flash (High) (exact model ID: `gemini-3.8-flash`)\n","du